From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tangenx <me@tangenx.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:43:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 042/128] feat: hide message menu items

Every option of the message context menu is registered with a stable
code, the parallel item/icon/option lists are filtered once at the end
of fillMessageMenu (covers all three call sites), and an editor screen
under tele > interface lists every item with a toggle. Stored codes
survive locale changes; unknown codes are ignored.

Ordering (0055) stays open: it needs a drag-and-drop editor and a
per-item position map, this pass only covers visibility.

Constraint: option codes are stable ints, not localized strings
Rejected: keying by menu title | titles break on app language change
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: narrow
Not-tested: interaction with the hidden-sensitive-content filter that also mutates the lists
